Curve equation is  y^2 = 7 x^6 + 6 x^5 + 5 x^4 + 4 x^3 + 3 x^2 + 2 x + 1


find_points:
  degree:       6
  coefficients: 1 2 3 4 5 6 7
  height bound: 10
  denominators from 1 to 10
  number of primes to consider:      30
  number of primes for sieving:      19
  number of primes for first stage:  11
  maximal number of `forbidden divisors': 30
  iterations for isolations of connected components: 10

Check if polynomial should be reversed for better performance:
  criteria are not met ==> don't reverse

Isolate the connected components:
  can restrict to the following intervals:
  [-10.000000, 10.000000] 

Obtain information from the polynomial mod 16:
  use all numerators for odd denominators

Find the points mod p for the first 30 odd primes p:
  use 11 primes for first stage:
    67 89 53 73 107 83 59 43 37 17 31
  use 8 primes for second stage:
    71 127 61 101 97 79 23 103

Now start the sieving procedure...

(-1 : 2 : 1)
(-1 : -2 : 1)
(0 : 1 : 1)
(0 : -1 : 1)
(8 : 2401 : 7)
(8 : -2401 : 7)

6 rational points found.

